From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 10:40:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS-Mythic ml513: report the effective TSO configuration at
 runtime
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A compiled-in config default is invisible to a binary grep, so there was
no way to know what the JIT was actually doing. This logs it from the
TSOHandlerConfig ctor:

  FEX: TSO config tso=1 halfbar=1 vector=0 memcpyset=0 rev=ml513

It exists because of an experiment it then disproved. ml512 flipped
VectorTSOEnabled and MemcpySetTSOEnabled to true — x86 orders SSE/AVX and
rep-movs accesses under TSO and FEX emits them unordered, which was the
last broad memory-ordering gap left after scalar TSO was audited clean.
Deploy was proven by this very line in both processes, and the Chromium
raster corruption was UNCHANGED.

Both defaults are therefore back at upstream (false) rather than kept: an
unproven change with a known cost muddies every later experiment, and
ordering every vector access taxes exactly the vector-heavy game
workloads that are the product. Recorded as a KNOWN ACCURACY GAP,
deliberately accepted — re-enable by flipping the two Config.json.in
defaults, and this line proves which way any build shipped.

Madeira-commit: 93c640cfbe7300831d9716ff1ab1ba5174c47132
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/Common/TSOHandlerConfig.h | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/TSOHandlerConfig.h b/Source/Windows/Common/TSOHandlerConfig.h
index f63478d..3691ae5 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/TSOHandlerConfig.h
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/TSOHandlerConfig.h
@@ -27,6 +27,26 @@ public:
     if (UnixLib::SetKernelUnalignedAtomicControl(Flags)) {
       LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: Kernel unaligned atomics enabled!");
     }
+
+    /* iOS-Mythic ml512/ml513: report the EFFECTIVE TSO configuration at
+     * runtime. A compiled-in config default is invisible to binary greps, so
+     * this line is the only way to know what the JIT is actually doing.
+     *
+     * ml512 flipped VectorTSOEnabled/MemcpySetTSOEnabled to true and the
+     * Chromium raster corruption was UNCHANGED; ml513 reverted both to the
+     * upstream default (false). KNOWN ACCURACY GAP, deliberately accepted:
+     * x86 orders SSE/AVX and rep-movs accesses under TSO and FEX emits them
+     * unordered, so a guest relying on per-location vector ordering without
+     * a scalar release would misbehave. Nothing observed needs it, and
+     * ordering every vector access taxes exactly the vector-heavy game
+     * workloads that are the product (Thumper). Re-enable by flipping the
+     * two Config.json.in defaults; this line proves which way it shipped. */
+    {
+      FEX_CONFIG_OPT(VecTSO, VECTORTSOENABLED);
+      FEX_CONFIG_OPT(MemcpyTSO, MEMCPYSETTSOENABLED);
+      LogMan::Msg::IFmt("FEX: TSO config tso={} halfbar={} vector={} memcpyset={} rev=ml513",
+                        TSOEnabled(), HalfBarrierTSOEnabled(), VecTSO(), MemcpyTSO());
+    }
   }
 
   FEXCore::ArchHelpers::Arm64::UnalignedHandlerType GetUnalignedHandlerType() const {
